I've sent the draft and report back. The file is `__PROJECT_ROOT__/docs/updates/2026-10-20/COMPARISON_DRAFT.md`. It's the only new file in the repo; nothing was committed, no models were called, and no credential files were read.

- **Before:** I used the v5 G0/G1/G2 runs (gpt-6-astra) as the baseline. They end on the same 702→1603.1 s window as S0, which makes the comparison direct. G0 used about 224 requests and 46M uncached-equivalent input tokens per simulated hour. Those per-hour figures are my own recalculation, since the old runs never recorded them.
- **Now:** S0 is at 62–116 requests and 8.6–11.5M tokens per simulated hour. That is roughly a quarter to a fifth of G0's cost. Quality metrics barely separate the groups in a 15-minute window.
- **Main caveat:** each request is still about the same size (around 190K tokens now vs 210K before). Today's request holds the whole factory state, where the old one held only part of it. The savings come from fewer requests, the single-step submit, and caching in P2. The model also changed, so not all of the drop can be credited to the harness.
- **Gaps:** the old runs have no summed count of rejected submissions. Their tardiness and idle are measured differently, so those rows are marked not comparable.
- **S1 Δ=300:** only 8 of its 22 sessions fell on the 300 s anchors. The cause of the other 14 is a placeholder.
- **Δ=900:** still running at 4 sessions and about 3.0M input tokens. Any figure from it is marked provisional.
- **Placeholders left:**
  - the one-line conclusion and the Δ recommendation;
